{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>Before I had finished.</b> Before I finish. And so every present-tense form — sometimes Scripture speaks in past tense, so it could write טֶרֶם כִּלִּיתִי, and sometimes it speaks in future tense, as when Job said — here is past tense: ״כָּכָה יַעֲשֶׂה אִיּוֹב״ (Job 1) — here is future tense, and the meaning of both is present tense, for Job would say: Perhaps my sons have sinned, etc., and he would do thus."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:16.626793108Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}